[507.5701, "o", "[bootstrap 18:45:34] running Copilot CLI (claude-opus-5.5, effort xhigh); report follows\r\n"]
[507.5701, "o", "\r\n"]
[507.5701, "o", "===== PR SHEPHERD REPORT =====\r\n"]
[509.1091, "o", "Re-triaging PR #13 first.\r\n"]
[509.1091, "o", "\r\n"]
[510.1486, "o", "Head is still `acb0ab8`, CI still failing, not DIRTY. Reading the failed job log.\r\n"]
[510.1486, "o", "\r\n"]
[510.9995, "o", "The PR only changes `deploy/utils/README.md`, but the failure is in `dump_docs` (YAML 1.1 quoting). Likely a base problem. Checking the base, merge base, and upstream for a fix.\r\n"]
[510.9995, "o", "\r\n"]
[511.8052, "o", "Merge base `07a80bb` dropped single-letter tokens from `_YAML11_AMBIGUOUS`. The next base commit, `367a899`, says it restores them. Checking that commit and the CI history on the base.\r\n"]
[511.8052, "o", "\r\n"]
[512.5076, "o", "Cause 2 (stale base), High confidence: `367a899` on `orka-demo/base` exactly reverts the breaking `07a80bb`. Next: rebase per step A. Backing up first.\r\n"]
[512.5076, "o", "\r\n"]
[513.6487, "o", "Backup verified. Reproducing the failure locally, then rebasing.\r\n"]
[513.6487, "o", "\r\n"]
[514.274, "o", "Rebase was clean and the commit is re-signed. Local pytest needs `pydantic` because the repo's warning filters import it. Checking what the CI workflow installs so I can match it.\r\n"]
[514.274, "o", "\r\n"]
[516.674, "o", "Pre-commit passes (exit 0). Confirming the remote head hasn't moved, then pushing with lease.\r\n"]
[516.674, "o", "\r\n"]
[517.4026, "o", "Pushed `2c2baf4`. Re-reading PR state and waiting briefly for the new CI run.\r\n"]
[517.4026, "o", "\r\n"]
[519.8026, "o", "CI is green on `2c2baf4` and the PR is CLEAN/MERGEABLE. Checking for an existing review brief that may now be out of date, then cleaning up.\r\n"]
