[650.1826, "o", "\u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;214m ⏩ the review run's log, sped up; the CodeRabbit lines are in demo 1 \u001b[0m\r\n"]
[650.4326, "o", "CodeRabbit's finding still applies at head (`M`/`G` use 1024). Next, I'll read the review rubric from upstream/main for self-review.\r\n"]
[652.1067, "o", "Rubric read. Now checking test markers, CI collection, replication (existing quantity parsers / `kubernetes.utils.parse_quantity`), and running the tests.\r\n"]
[654.5067, "o", "Pre-commit passes. Before committing, a fresh subagent will confirm the diff fixes exactly the listed item and nothing else.\r\n"]
[656.9067, "o", "**CONFIRMED**\r\n"]
[656.9067, "o", "\r\n"]
[656.9212, "o", "- **(a)** `/tmp/work/dynamo/deploy/utils/quantity.py` changes only `M` and `G` to `1000**2` and `1000**3`, matching Kubernetes decimal semantics.\r\n"]
[656.9413, "o", "- **(b)** New `M`/`G` assertions pass with current source: **15 passed**. With old multipliers, all three new assertions fail with `1048576`/`1073741824`.\r\n"]
[656.9656, "o", "- **(c)** Diff contains only those multiplier fixes and regression assertions. Other suffixes are unchanged; `git diff --check` passes.\r\n"]
[656.9656, "o", "\r\n"]
[657.3266, "o", "No problem found in the diff. The normal pytest command initially loaded a stale same-second `.pyc`; forcing current source confirmed the passing result.Confirmed. Re-checking the PR head and approvals, then committing (signed, signed-off) and pushing.\r\n"]
